The '''infernal cape''' is the most powerful melee cape in terms of overall bonuses, awarded for defeating [[TzKal-Zuk]] in the [[Inferno]]. It surpasses its predecessor, the [[fire cape]], boasting greater melee attack and strength bonuses, along with slightly higher defensive bonuses. In spite of this, it is still surpassed by the [[Ardougne cloak]]s [[Ardougne cloak 3|3]] and [[Ardougne cloak 4|4]] in stab attack and prayer bonuses, and by the [[mythical cape]] in crush attack.

An infernal cape can be exchanged for a chance of obtaining the [[Jal-Nib-Rek]] pet by speaking to [[TzHaar-Ket-Keh]]. Like killing [[TzKal-Zuk]], there is a 1/100 chance of obtaining the pet this way. If the player already has the pet, capes cannot be exchanged.

An infernal cape can be combined with the [[max cape]] to change its appearance by turning it into the [[infernal max cape]].

As of 1 October 2026, there are '''176,365''' <!--page=7055--> accounts that have obtained an infernal cape.

If the player dies a PvP death at level 20 Wilderness or below and the item is [[Items Kept on Death|unprotected]], it will remain in the player's inventory; however, the item will be in a broken, unusable state and must be repaired by using it on [[Perdu]] and paying him {{NoCoins|225,000}} [[coins]].

If the player dies a PvP death above level 20 Wilderness and the item is [[Items Kept on Death|unprotected]], it will be converted to coins. To prevent this, a [[Trouver parchment]] and a payment of {{NoCoins|500,000}} coins can be given to [[Perdu]] in order to permanently [[(l)|lock]] the item. The locked item will remain in the player's inventory; however, the item will be in a mangled, unusable state and must be repaired by using it on Perdu and paying him {{NoCoins|500,000}} coins.

While equipping the fire cape will grant players the [[fiery (attribute)|fiery attribute]] and will therefore make them susceptible to the extra damage from the special effect of [[pearl bolts (e)]], the infernal cape does not grant this attribute.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Arcane|url=https://twitter.com/JagexArcane/status/1455113239860219907|date=1 November 2021|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/98674|archivedate=4 November 2021|quote=TIL Pearl bolts do bonus damage if the opponent is wearing a fire cape. Just another thing that makes Inferno worth doing.}}

