==Trivia==
[[File:Infernal cape IRL.png|thumb|Real life version of Infernal cape seen in The Inferno's behind-the-scenes video]]
*The first player to obtain the cape was ''Woox'', who claimed the cape two days after release.{{CiteTwitter|author=Old School RuneScape|url=https://twitter.com/OldSchoolRS/status/870939670363996160|date=3 June 2017|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/106851|archivedate=29 May 2020|quote=A MASSIVE CONGRATULATIONS TO @WooxSolo FOR DEFEATING THE INFERNO! First in the world!}}
**As the first player to complete the Inferno, he was awarded a real-life version of the infernal cape, as well as a [[rsw:RuneFest 2017|RuneFest 2017]] ticket with full-expenses paid travel and lifetime membership.{{CiteForum|author=Mod Ronan|url=http://services.runescape.com/m=news/the-inferno?oldschool=1|title=The Inferno|forum=Old School RuneScape|postdate=June 1, 2017}}
*The infernal cape and [[fire cape]], along with their max cape variants, are the only capes to have an animated texture whilst wearing them.
*As of [[13 November]] [[2020]], 1,692 infernal capes have been removed from users who obtained an infernal cape illegitimately by having another person complete the Inferno for them.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Tyran|url=https://twitter.com/JagexTyran/status/1327212531887329282|date=13 November 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/99809|archivedate=13 November 2020|quote=Happy Friday 13th, we're rolling out a further 260 offences for illegitimate Infernal Capes this week. That's 1,692 in total so far.}}
* Prior to an unknown update, defeating TzKal-Zuk with a full inventory resulted in the infernal cape and tokkul not being given to the player at all. However, the cape's [[collection log]] slot would still be unlocked. Currently, doing so results in both being placed on the ground for the player to pick up.
**If TzKal-Zuk is defeated with only one inventory slot open, the infernal cape will be given to the player, but their tokkul will be dropped on the ground.

